   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to including electronic\nmessaging texts as a form of telemarketing communication",
    "basePrintNo": "S3941",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3941-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 5,
       "fullName": "Jim Gaughran",
       "imgName": "1042_Jim_Gaughran.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1222,
       "sessionMemberId": 1807,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "GAUGHRAN"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §399-z, Gen Bus L",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3941\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to including elec-\ntronic messaging texts as a form of telemarketing communication\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to add electronic messaging texts to the\ndefinition of telemarketing.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subdivisions h, i, j, k, 1, m of section 399-z of the\ngeneral business law to add electronic messaging texts to the definition\nof telemarketing; and adds a subdivision n of section 399-z of the\ngeneral business law that adds a new definition for electronic messaging\ntext.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTelemarketing, commonly known as robocalling, has become a frequent\nunwanted nuisance for consumers across New York State and the country.\nin current New York State law, the definition of telemarketing in the\ngeneral business law only includes telephone calls. However, with the\nadvancements made in technology since this law was enacted, electronic\ntext messages have become common practice in telemarketing. Consumers\nshould be protected from excessive telemarketing in all forms, including\ntext messages, which this bill accomplishes by adding electronic messag-\ning text to the definition of telemarketing.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect thirty days after it shall become law.\n",
